# Git commit & branch

Only commit / push / create branches when the user explicitly asks. Never commit proactively.

Read and follow `.agents/skills/git/SKILL.md` (also linked as `.cursor/skills/git` and `.claude/skills/git`).

## Message format

```
type[/scope[/subscope]][+scope]: summary
```

**Types (only these):** `feat` · `fix` · `refactor` · `chore`

- No `style` or `docs` type — visual polish is `refactor`; documentation is `chore/docs`
- Scope from allowlist only; omit only for genuinely extension-wide changes
- Never invent a new scope — ask before adding one
- Nested `/`; combined `+` when one commit spans two scopes
- Summary: lowercase first word, imperative, no trailing period, ≤ ~50 chars (hard ~60)
- Single-line subject by default; body only when why isn’t obvious

## Scope allowlist

| Scope | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `preview` | Right column |
| `edit` | full screen edit mode |
| `header` | header in the full screen mode |
| `docs` | README, store listing copy, publisher/setup docs (`chore/docs`) |
| `backend` | Other backend related changes |
| `engine` | Image Extraction engine |
| `tests` | Jest / test files |
| `agents` | `.cursor/agents`, `.cursor/skills`, `.cursor/rules` |
| `gitignore` | `.gitignore` |

## Branches

`type/scope[-short-slug]` — same type/scope as the primary commit.

## Atomic commits & safety

One coherent change per commit; `git add <paths>` not `git add .`. No force-push / `--no-verify` / secrets / git config / push unless asked.
